        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0197" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg93"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.42157 Detrodt/33</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Canada (Boal) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1297</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-03-23">March 23,
                        1933</date>.<lb/>[Received March 24.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to instruction
                    No. 706 of September 24, 1932, (file No. 711.42157 Detroit/25) and other
                    correspondence, regarding operations to be conducted in Canadian waters in
                    connection with the dredging of certain shoal areas in the St. Clair River, and
                    to report the receipt of note No. 27 of March 21, 1933, from the Department of
                    External Affairs, in which the Canadian Government grants the necessary
                    permission to carry out the proposed works, subject, however, to certain
                    important conditions.</p>
                <p>Copy of the note in question is transmitted herewith.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierre de L. Boal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d68-a1.xml" xpointer="d68-a1"/>
            </div>
